<main class="content" id="content-area">

  <!-- SCREEN 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div id="content-1" class="screen-content">
    <div class="screen-tag"><span class="screen-number">01 / 10</span> Onboarding</div>
    <h1 class="screen-title">Splash</h1>
    <p class="screen-oneliner">The brand says hello before the product does anything. A holding state — not a loader.</p>

    <div class="section-label">Function</div>
    <div class="function-block">
      Cold start state. Loads the user session, fetches card data, and routes to the onboarding flow or home. Visible for ~600ms on a warm start, up to 2 seconds on cold. No spinner. No progress bar. The wordmark is the animation.
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Screen elements</div>
    <ul class="elements-list">
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Full-bleed background in Bloop primary — deep verdant green (#1F6E5A).</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Centred Bloop wordmark in white. The two 'o' characters are optically oversized — a quiet visual reference to a tap. Custom-cut letterform.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Wordmark breathing animation — scale 1.0 → 1.025 → 1.0 on a 2.4s ease-in-out loop.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Status bar in light-content style. Nothing else competes for attention on this screen.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Copy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Wordmark</td><td class="copy-text">bloop</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Loading state</td><td class="copy-text">(no copy — animation only)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Error fallback (3s+ overrun)</td><td class="copy-text">Hmm. Give us one more second.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="section-label">Motion notes</div>
    <ul class="elements-list">
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Wordmark fades in over 200ms on launch (opacity 0 → 1, ease-out).</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Breathing scale loop runs while session loads.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>On route: wordmark scales up to 1.15 and fades out as the next screen slides in — 300ms ease-out.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-label">Brand note</div>
    <div class="note-block">
      <strong>This screen does not have to earn its place through utility.</strong> Every other screen in the app justifies its design with function. The splash is the only moment that is unapologetically a brand gesture. Resist the urge to add sub-copy, a spinner, or a progress indicator. The restraint is the statement.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SCREEN 2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div id="content-2" class="screen-content" style="display:none">
    <div class="screen-tag"><span class="screen-number">02 / 10</span> Onboarding</div>
    <h1 class="screen-title">Welcome / Value prop carousel</h1>
    <p class="screen-oneliner">Three slides. Eight seconds. The user either gets it — or they don't need to.</p>

    <div class="section-label">Function</div>
    <div class="function-block">
      Shown once, immediately after the splash, before any account creation. A horizontal carousel of three screens, each making one argument for why Bloop exists. Dismissible from any slide. Swipeable. Auto-advances after 5s per slide if idle.
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Screen elements</div>
    <ul class="elements-list">
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Top 55% — editorial full-bleed visual. Slide 1: two Bloop cards mid-exchange. Slide 2: phone screen with a Bloop profile. Slide 3: a tap notification arriving. All commissioned, not stock.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Bottom 45% — white card content area with rounded top corners.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Slide headline (display serif, 22pt), body (13pt, muted), progress dots, primary CTA, ghost secondary.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Progress dots: active dot is a pill (20px wide), inactive dots are circles (6px). Animates between slides.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Skip link top-right — always visible, exits to sign up.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy — Slide 1</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Copy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Headline</td><td class="copy-text">One tap. You exist on their phone now.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Body</td><td class="copy-text">NFC contact card that shares everything — or only what you want.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">CTA</td><td class="copy-text">Next</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy — Slide 2</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Copy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Headline</td><td class="copy-text">Different place, different you.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Body</td><td class="copy-text">Switch profiles for the gallery, the office, the party. Same chip, three cards.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">CTA</td><td class="copy-text">Next</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy — Slide 3</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Copy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Headline</td><td class="copy-text">Remember everyone you actually meet.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Body</td><td class="copy-text">Bloop logs every tap — who, when, where — so you don't have to.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">CTA (final slide)</td><td class="copy-text">Get started</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Ghost link</td><td class="copy-text">Sign in instead</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Skip link (persistent)</td><td class="copy-text">Skip</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="section-label">Brand note</div>
    <div class="note-block">
      <strong>Three slides maximum, one argument each.</strong> Most onboarding carousels try to say everything. Bloop says three things and stops. The editorial visuals do more work than the copy — if the image doesn't make someone want to keep reading, the copy doesn't get a chance. Commission, don't stock.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SCREEN 3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div id="content-3" class="screen-content" style="display:none">
    <div class="screen-tag"><span class="screen-number">03 / 10</span> Onboarding</div>
    <h1 class="screen-title">Sign up — phone or email</h1>
    <p class="screen-oneliner">The smallest possible commitment. One field. One tap.</p>

    <div class="section-label">Function</div>
    <div class="function-block">
      Entry point for account creation. Supports phone (default) and email as toggle options. Phone sends an OTP via SMS; email sends a magic link. No password ever created. Either method routes to OTP verification (Screen 04). Apple Sign In and Google Sign In as tertiary options below the fold.
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Screen elements</div>
    <ul class="elements-list">
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Small Bloop wordmark centred at top — confirms brand context without the splash drama.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Screen headline + one-line subhead.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Segmented control: Phone (default active) / Email.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Phone state: country code picker + phone number field. Auto-formats as user types.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Email state: single email field with format validation.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Primary CTA — disabled until field has valid input.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Terms caption below CTA — 9pt, muted. Not blocking, not modal. Just present.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Hairline divider + 'or' separator + Apple / Google SSO options below.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Copy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Headline</td><td class="copy-text">Let's get you a bloop</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Subhead</td><td class="copy-text">Takes about two minutes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Tab — phone</td><td class="copy-text">Phone</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Tab — email</td><td class="copy-text">Email</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Phone field label</td><td class="copy-text">Mobile number</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Phone placeholder</td><td class="copy-text">Your number</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Email field label</td><td class="copy-text">Email address</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Email placeholder</td><td class="copy-text">Your email</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">CTA</td><td class="copy-text">Send the code</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Terms caption</td><td class="copy-text">By continuing you agree to our Terms and Privacy Policy.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">SSO divider</td><td class="copy-text">or</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Apple SSO</td><td class="copy-text">Continue with Apple</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Google SSO</td><td class="copy-text">Continue with Google</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="el-name">Sign-in redirect</td><td class="copy-text">Already have an account? Sign in</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="section-label">Brand note</div>
    <div class="note-block">
      <strong>"Let's get you a bloop"</strong> — using 'bloop' as the object (a noun) rather than a product name establishes the language from the very first interaction. Users learn the vocabulary before they've even signed up. The CTA "Send the code" is a verb that explains the action, not a generic "Continue."
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SCREEN 4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div id="content-4" class="screen-content" style="display:none">
    <div class="screen-tag"><span class="screen-number">04 / 10</span> Onboarding</div>
    <h1 class="screen-title">OTP verification</h1>
    <p class="screen-oneliner">Six boxes. One moment of trust between the user and the number they gave us.</p>

    <div class="section-label">Function</div>
    <div class="function-block">
      Receives the 6-digit OTP sent to the user's phone or a magic link click for email. Auto-submits when all six digits are entered — no manual "verify" tap required. Shows a resend option after 30 seconds. Incorrect code shakes the boxes and clears them.
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Screen elements</div>
    <ul class="elements-list">
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Back arrow (returns to sign-up screen, phone/email preserved).</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Headline, personalised with the last 4 digits of the phone or the email domain.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>6 individual digit input boxes. Active box has accent-green border. Filled boxes show green digit. Cursor is hidden — digit jumps to next box automatically.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Resend link — disabled for first 30 seconds with countdown: "Resend in 28s".</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Primary CTA — auto-triggers on last digit, but also manually tappable.</li>
      <li><span class="el-bullet"></span>Error state: boxes shake (200ms wobble animation), border turns red briefly, all clear.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-label">UX copy</div>
    <table class="copy-table">
